    "body": "Given: a removeUrl is set with `setSettings` and the user clicks \"Remove\" from the tab menu\r\nExpected: The Remove form button is not activated until `setValidityState(true)` is called\r\nActual: The Remove form button is activated after a timeout no matter what. Subsequent calls to `setValidityState(false)` do not deactivate the form button\r\n\r\nI tested using the example code here: https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoftteams/platform/tabs/how-to/create-tab-pages/removal-page\r\n\r\nMy specific code, I am using older js, not es6, but that shouldn't affect anything: \r\n\r\n```html\r\n<html>\r\n<head>\r\n  <script src= 'https://statics.teams.cdn.office.net/sdk/v1.5.2/js/MicrosoftTeams.min.js'></script>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n  <button onclick=\"onClick()\">Delete this tab and all underlying data?</button>\r\n  <script>\r\n    microsoftTeams.initialize();\r\n    microsoftTeams.settings.registerOnRemoveHandler(function(removeEvent) {\r\n      // Here you can designate the tab content to be removed and/or archived.\r\n        microsoftTeams.settings.getSettings(function(settings) {\r\n        });\r\n        removeEvent.notifySuccess();\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    function onClick() {\r\n        microsoftTeams.settings.setValidityState(true);\r\n    }\r\n  </script>\r\n</body>\r\n</html>\r\n```",
